# November 24, 2026: Carnegie libraries of eastern and southern New York outside New York City, the second batch of a
# pass asked for by the owner to put the buildings Andrew Carnegie paid for on the map. Started from Wikipedia's "List
# of Carnegie libraries in New York". This batch: fifteen the Atlas did not have, in the Hudson Valley, the Mohawk
# Valley, the North Country, Westchester and Rockland, Long Island, Schenectady and Alfred, with the site of Ossining's
# (torn down). Sources opened in this session: Wikipedia as raw text, and through the web fetch tool the libraries' own
# pages (hours, histories), the colleges' pages, local papers and historical pages.
# Pins: OpenStreetMap library points and ArcGIS geocoder points for the street addresses, looked at on the leaf-off aerial.
