  'The Catskill Public Library was founded in 1893, and its neo-classical building at Franklin and Bridge Streets was paid for by a Carnegie grant of 1901. It has three floors and is reached by ramp only on the lower one. In 2026 the library announced plans, with a state downtown grant, to restore the lower-floor Carnegie Community Hall and add a children\'s wing with a sunken garden.',
  'The neo-classical library on the corner of Franklin and Bridge Streets, with a historic linden tree by it. Still the village library, open to anyone in its hours. Interior not checked.',
